.TH AENIGMA-VPN-SERVER-HOST 8 "2026-08-13" "aenigma 5.0.0" "Aenigma Administration Scripts"
.SH NAME
aenigma-vpn-server-host \- assign a static VPN IP and DNS hostname
to an OpenVPN client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aenigma-vpn-server-host
.B \-c
.I CLIENT_NAME
.B \-d
.I DOMAIN
.B \-i
.I IP
.B \-n
.I NETMASK
.br
.B aenigma-vpn-server-host
.B \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aenigma-vpn-server-host
assigns a fixed VPN IP address to a specific client via OpenVPN's
client-config-dir mechanism, and, if
.BR dnsmasq (8)
has been configured for the server's domain by
.BR aenigma-vpn-dns (8),
registers a corresponding hostname for that client in the local
hosts file used by
.BR dnsmasq .
.PP
The script performs the following actions:
.IP \(bu 2
Verifies that the server's client-config-dir,
.IR /etc/openvpn/ccd/ DOMAIN ,
already exists, and exits with an error if it does not, since it
must have been created by
.BR aenigma-vpn-server (8)
beforehand.
.IP \(bu 2
Creates (if absent) or updates the per-client configuration file
.IR /etc/openvpn/ccd/ DOMAIN / CLIENT_NAME .
Any existing
.B ifconfig-push
line in that file is removed, and a new one is appended assigning
.I IP
and
.I NETMASK
to the client; any other directives already present in the file are
left untouched.
.IP \(bu 2
If
.IR /etc/openvpn/ DOMAIN /dnsmasq\-hosts
exists (indicating
.BR dnsmasq (8)
has been configured for this domain via
.BR aenigma-vpn-dns (8)),
adds an entry mapping
.I IP
to the hostname
.IR CLIENT_NAME . DOMAIN ,
unless a matching entry already exists, and restarts
.BR dnsmasq .
If that file does not exist, DNS hostname registration is skipped
with a notice, and the rest of the script still completes normally.
.PP
.B aenigma-vpn-server-host
must be run as root, and is intended to be run on the VPN
.B server
host, after the corresponding client certificate has already been
issued via
.BR aenigma-vpn-server-client (8).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " CLIENT_NAME"
Name of the client to assign a static IP to. Must match the common
name used when the client's certificate was issued via
.BR aenigma-vpn-server-client (8)
for OpenVPN to apply this configuration to the correct connecting
client. Required.
.TP
.BI \-d " DOMAIN"
Domain name of the already-configured VPN server (as set up by
.BR aenigma-vpn-server (8)).
Required.
.TP
.BI \-i " IP"
Static VPN IP address to assign to the client, e.g.
.IR 10.8.0.10 .
Required.
.TP
.BI \-n " NETMASK"
Netmask for the VPN network, e.g.
.IR 255.255.255.0 .
Should match the netmask used when the server was configured via
.BR aenigma-vpn-server (8).
Required.
.TP
.B \-h
Display a usage summary and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The client's static IP was assigned successfully, whether or not DNS
hostname registration was applicable.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid or missing arguments, the script was not run as root, or
.I /etc/openvpn/ccd/ DOMAIN
does not exist.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/openvpn/ccd/ DOMAIN / CLIENT_NAME
Per-client OpenVPN configuration file. Created if absent; its
.B ifconfig-push
directive is replaced on each run, other directives are preserved.
.TP
.I /etc/openvpn/ DOMAIN /dnsmasq\-hosts
Additional hosts file consulted by
.BR dnsmasq ,
as configured by
.BR aenigma-vpn-dns (8).
An entry for
.IR CLIENT_NAME . DOMAIN
is appended if not already present. Not created by this script if
absent.
.SH EXAMPLES
Assign a static IP and hostname to a client named
.I john
on server
.IR example.com :
.PP
.RS
.EX
sudo aenigma-vpn-server-host \-c john \-d example.com \e
    \-i 10.8.0.10 \-n 255.255.255.0
.EE
.RE
.SH NOTES
Neither
.I CLIENT_NAME
nor
.I IP
is validated against the client certificates already issued via
.BR aenigma-vpn-server-client (8),
nor against other static IP assignments already made via this
script for the same
.IR DOMAIN .
It is the operator's responsibility to ensure
.I CLIENT_NAME
matches an existing, issued client certificate, and that
.I IP
is not already assigned to a different client; this script does not
detect or warn about duplicate IP assignments across the
client-config-dir.
.PP
The hostname-existence check against
.I dnsmasq\-hosts
.RB ( "grep -q \(dq$HOSTNAME\(dq" )
matches the hostname text anywhere in the file, not as a
whole-line or whole-field match. A hostname that is a substring of
another already-registered hostname (or vice versa) may be
incorrectly treated as already present, silently skipping the
intended new entry.
.PP
If a client's static IP needs to change, re-running this script with
a new
.I IP
value correctly replaces the
.B ifconfig-push
line in the client's ccd file, but does
.B not
remove or update the client's
.B previous
IP-to-hostname mapping in
.IR dnsmasq\-hosts ;
the old entry is left in place alongside whatever new entry (if any)
results, potentially leaving a stale or duplicate hostname mapping.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR openvpn (8),
.BR dnsmasq (8),
.BR aenigma-vpn-server (8),
.BR aenigma-vpn-server-client (8),
.BR aenigma-vpn-dns (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Romulus-Emanuel Ruja <romulus.ruja@aenigma.ro>
